Cell["\<\
Now in theory, if I can manipulate C++\[OpenCurlyQuote]s normal distribution \
to make this distribution work, we should be good to go. The standard normal \
distribution does not have a constant offset however. So I should see if I \
can use some stats tricks to artificially construct my offset normal \
distribution. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.794072429972011*^9, 3.7940724638424473`*^9}, {
  3.7940725267475104`*^9, 
  3.794072540249025*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4d98b1f0-f166-472d-8bc1-\
1b6aa795d457"],

